# Hallmark — no AI-looking UI

When designing or editing frontend UI, refuse generic LLM aesthetics. Prefer craft that feels intentional and brand-specific.

For full protocol (themes, macrostructures, slop-test, study/audit/redesign), read and follow the `hallmark` skill at `.cursor/skills/hallmark/SKILL.md`.

## Hard bans (never ship)

1. **Purple/indigo gradient heroes** — no purple→blue/pink gradients, no glow blobs as the main idea
2. **Default fonts as display** — never Inter, Roboto, Open Sans, Arial, or system-ui for display; pair a distinctive display face with a refined body
3. **Centered everything** — bias the layout; break symmetry on purpose
4. **Icon-tile feature cards** — no rounded card + colored icon square + 2-line title + 3-line blurb + "Learn more →"
5. **AI nav chrome** — no wordmark-left / links-center / CTA-right sticky hairline nav as the default
6. **Gradient pill CTAs** — solid fill or outline, single hue
7. **Sparkle/emoji badges** — use a real icon set or nothing
8. **Invented metrics** — no fake "10×", "50k teams", Trustpilot stars unless the user supplied them
9. **Italic display headers** — headings stay roman; italic only in body emphasis
10. **Cards in heroes** — no card chrome in the first viewport unless it is the interaction surface

## Required craft

- One clear visual direction; OKLCH tokens; one anchor hue; accent under ~5%
- Named spacing scale (multiples of 4)
- Asymmetric layout bias over template centering
- Real imagery / product context over decorative abstract gradients
- Motion: exponential ease-out + `prefers-reduced-motion` alternative
- Mobile: no horizontal scroll at 320–768px

## Verbs

- Default build → follow hallmark Design flow
- `hallmark audit` → punch list only, no edits
- `hallmark redesign` → new structure, same content/brand
- `hallmark study` → extract DNA from URL/screenshot, never copy pixels
